        String jma_preliminary_publication "Kobayashi, S., Y. Kosaka, J. Chiba, T. Tokuhiro, Y. Harada, C. Kobayashi, and H. Naoe, 2021: JRA-3Q: Japanese Reanalysis for Three Quarters of a Century. Joint WCRP-WWRP Symposium on Data Assimilation and Reanalysis/ECMWF Annual Seminar 2021, online, 13-17 September 2021, O4-2.";
        String jma_preliminary_publication_url "https://symp-bonn2021.sciencesconf.org/data/355900.pdf";
        String jma_primary_publication "Kosaka, Y., S. Kobayashi, Y. Harada, C. Kobayashi, H. Naoe, K. Yoshimoto, M. Harada, N. Goto, J. Chiba, K. Miyaoka, R. Sekiguchi, M. Deushi, H. Kamahori, T. Nakaegawa, T. Y. Tanaka, T. Tokuhiro, Y. Sato, Y. Matsushita, and K. Onogi, 2024: The JRA-3Q Reanalysis. J. Meteor. Soc. Japan, 102, 1-168 (DOI: 10.2151/jmsj.2024-004). (Reference to JRA-3Q data in scientific or technical papers should cite this comprehensive report.)";
        String jma_primary_publication_url "https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jmsj/advpub/0/advpub_2024-004/_article/-char/ja/";
        String jma_data_source_acknowledgement "This report references JRA-3Q reanalysis data from the Japan Meteorological Agency.";
        String jma_ncar_cooperative_agreement "Letter dated 6 October 2023: Dr. Thomas Hauser (CISL Director, Associate NCAR Director) requests approval from JMA to archive JRA-3Q data in NCAR's Research Data archive (RDA) in alignment with the Terms and Conditions of Request Submission and Archival of Data to the RDA presented at https://rda.ucar.edu/resources/daas/terms-and-conditions/. The JRA-3Q data will be securely stored on NCAR disk storage with a tape backup copy maintained on NCAR's Quasar tape system. When accessing JRA-3Q data from NCAR's High Perforamnce Computing systems or from web data gateways, users will implicity agree to the conditions of use and conditions of the assigned data license provided by JMA. NCAR will monitor its data usage and share the metrics with JMA when called upon to do so. NCAR serves a broad research and education community, is managed by the University Corporation for Atmospheric Research (UCAR) and sponsored by the National Science Foundation (NSF). Letter dated 24 October 2023: Mr. Gouki Chiba (Director-General, Information Infrastructure Department, Japan Meteorological Agency) acting for Mr. Obayashi Masanori (Director-General, Japan Meteorological Agency) approves JMA provision of JRA-3Q data to the National Center for Atmospheric Research (NCAR) under the Creative Commons License CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The intellectual property rights of the datasets belong exclusively to JMA.";
        String jma_jra3q_cobe_sst "In JRA-3Q, the sea surface temperature (SST) specified as the lower boundary condition is the Centennial In Situ Observation-based Estimates of the Variability of SSTs and Marine Meteorological Variables Version 2 (COBE-SST2) with a resolution of 1 degree based on in situ observations until May 1985 and the Merged Satellite and In-Situ Data Global Daily Sea Surface Temperature (MGDSST) with a resolution of 0.25 degree based on satellite observations since June 1985. To enable evaluation of changes in product characteristics following the switch from COBE-SST2 to MGDSST, a sub-product using COBE-SST2 (JRA-3Q-COBE) is also provided for the period from June 1985 to December 1990.";
