        String jma_local_issues_with_sea_ice_parameters "JRA-3Q contains errors in sea ice cover for the period June 1985 to April 2013. Areas within approximately 250 km of the sea ice margin (fractional coverage of 0.1 or above) in both northern and southern hemispheres where ice cover should be 0.0 instead average roughly 0.15. Notable associated effects include increased surface upward short-wave radiation flux, reduced surface upward long-wave radiation flux, reduced sensible heat flux, reduced latent heat flux, reduced 2 meter temperature, and increased 2 meter relative humidity. Any or all of these parameters may be part of this data group (anl_surf). The error in sea ice cover represents only a fraction of the standard deviation in year-to-year variation, and effects on JRA-3Q quality are local and minor. The relevant JMA documentation is https://jra.kishou.go.jp/JRA-3Q/document/JRA-3Q_qualityissue_20221209_en.pdf.";
